<title>RUSSIA: Russian GAZ Oct vehicle output edges up.</title>
<headline>Russian GAZ Oct vehicle output edges up.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1996-11-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russia's second-largest vehicle maker AO GAZ  increased production six percent in October on a year ago to 18,700 vehicles and expects 1996 annual output to rise mainly on microbus output, GAZ said on Monday.</p>
<p>It gave the following data in a statement to Reuters:</p>
<p>				  October		   Total</p>
<p>			     1996     1995	  1996E	1995</p>
<p> All Trucks		7,442    6,431	 84,766   81,619</p>
<p> Gazelle model</p>
<p>  3302 1.5 tonne	 5,066    4,456	 57,611   57,520</p>
<p>  Microbus 2705	  1,391	  0	 13,559	102</p>
<p>  Microbus 3221	    914	  0	  4,337	  0</p>
<p>Cars (Volga</p>
<p>  medium-size sedan)  11,252   11,202	124,162  118,673</p>
<p> Total		    18,694   17,633	208,928  200,202</p>
<p>NOTE - Full name AO Gorkovsky Avtomobilny Zavod.</p>
<p>--Peter Henderson, Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
</text>
